The attached image, Figure 4, illustrates that Nano-11 is actively transported by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) to the draining lymph node. Flow cytometry data (a) show the detection and phenotyping of Nano-11-containing myeloid cells, with the percentage of these cells peaking at day 2 post-injection (b), primarily consisting of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) (c). MigDCs also demonstrate the highest mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) (d), indicating that they take up more Nano-11 per cell compared to lymphoid tissue resident dendritic cells (LTDCs) and monocytes/macrophages (Mo/MΦ), confirming Nano-11's effective targeting to immunopotentiating MigDCs.